     1	# The issuer implements the registered issuance lifecycle (2026-10-29)
     2	
     3	> **Status: OWNER DECISION**, by the owner instance (Claude Opus 5.5). It corrects an owner defect found by the
     4	> Levadura consistency panel (finding c016, `levadura_salvaje/docs/tessera-a11-canary-scorecard.md`). The service
     5	> resolution S4 (`docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:23`) and the issuer failed every request 24 hours after
     6	> acceptance. The registered lifecycle (A2.1, A2.3; parameters in A9.2) has no such deadline, and it makes "every
     7	> timely-eligible attempt ships" an obligation on the implementation (`phase-0-prereg-amendment-2.md:143-145`).
     8	> Registered text governs. This changes no registered sentence. It changes owner documents and code.
     9	
    10	## What is registered
    11	
    12	- Parameters (A9.2; frozen profile §1): δ = 72 h, ε = 24 h, k = 6, **N = 3**, S = 24 h.
    13	- **Attempts.** Issuance makes at most N attempts. Each attempt has its own declared issue time, frames and
    14	  signatures (A2.3, `phase-0-prereg-amendment-2.md:259-268`).
    15	- **Expiry.** An attempt expires when wall time passes `declared + δ + S`, *except* that timely-latched eligibility
    16	  excludes expiry. Eligible or finalizing, shipped, and expired or refused are mutually exclusive states
    17	  (A2.3; A2.1 `:131-135`).
    18	- **Eligibility** is chain-side and stateless: the attempt's evidence meets `T ≤ declared + δ` and
    19	  `confirmed ≤ declared + δ` (the frozen verifier's rows 12.2 and 12.3, `service/verifier/tessera_verify/verify.py:236-237`).
    20	  Once eligible, later packaging or scheduling delay cannot expire it.
    21	- **Refusal.** Exhausting N attempts ends issuance in an explicit refusal, durably recorded (A2.3).
    22	- **Window.** An attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped (A9, issuer invariant, `:422`).
    23	- **No SLA in this set.** A hard latency bound may enter only as a deployment-profile item "with monitoring and an
    24	  explicit violation outcome" (A2.1, `:139-142`). It may not kill an eligible attempt.
    25	
    26	## What the issuer does
    27	
    28	1. A request holds a list of attempts. Attempt 1 starts at acceptance, with declared time = the acceptance reading.
    29	2. On each poll, for each open attempt, the issuer first evaluates eligibility from the attempt's chain evidence
    30	   (the predicate of rows 12.2 and 12.3). If it holds, the issuer **latches** the attempt, with a durable
    31	   compare-and-set write. A latched attempt is never expired. It goes on to assembly, the pre-ship checks and
    32	   COMPLETE.
    33	3. Only if the attempt is not latched, and the wall reading (taken after the record read, CF2-02) is past
    34	   `declared + δ + S`, does the attempt expire. Then, if fewer than N attempts have been made, and signing is still
    35	   open (the signing stop and `sign_by`), a new attempt starts with a fresh declared time, fresh frames and fresh
    36	   signatures. Otherwise the request ends **REFUSED** with a recorded reason (`ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED` or
    37	   `SIGNING_CLOSED`).
    38	4. The latch write is the race against expiry, so it follows CF2-01's rule: the latch counts only if it was decided at
    39	   least `WRITE_LEASE_S` before that attempt's `declared + δ + S`. The chain predicate is stateless, so a
    40	   late-observed eligible attempt can still be latched on a later poll. A2.1 says a lag beyond S *may* be refused.
    41	   This design latches whenever the predicate holds before expiry is decided, which is the more permissive of the
    42	   two registered choices.
    43	5. Nothing fails a request at 24 hours. The 30-day retention runs from the request's end (S5, unchanged).
    44	6. A request's end can be up to N × (δ + S), nominally 12 days (A2.3), plus the stated clock tolerance.
    45	
    46	## Owner documents to change
    47	
    48	- **S4:** "usually complete within 3 hours" stays as a stated, unguaranteed figure. The 24-hour FAILED is removed.
    49	  The end is COMPLETE, or REFUSED when attempts are exhausted or signing has closed, at up to N × (δ + S).
    50	- **L1:** acceptance stops at least δ + S + 24 h before signing stops, so a first attempt always has its full
