docs/reviews/issuer/codex.log:14:Repo /home/tony/projects/tessera. Non-author code review of the V1 issuer in service/issuer/ (design: service/issuer/DESIGN.md; client behaviour it must implement: docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md, stamped; contract: docs/V1-SERVICE-CONTRACT.md; frozen profile: docs/V1-PROFILE.md §4, §6-§8, §15; lessons: prototype/e2e/FINDINGS.md E-01..E-06). It is tested only locally against stand-ins; nothing is deployed. Priorities: (1) any path that can SHIP a receipt that is incomplete, fails verification, falls outside the issuance window or stop margin, or was signed without being logged; (2) any path where a request's outcome differs from the stamped resolutions (refusal finality, request-key idempotence, 24 h failure, 30-day expiry, per-credential access, content retention and deletion); (3) E-02: late or unrequested signer responses not recorded, or a retry that signs again when a complete verified set exists; (4) Terraform: any IAM grant broader than needed, especially any KMS permission for the issuer, public S3 access, or a pre-signed URL that outlives the 30-day retention or leaks to another credential; (5) concurrency: two pollers or duplicate submissions racing. Run its tests (service/issuer/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q). Findings IS-NN with severity, file:line, a concrete failing scenario, and a fix. Do not edit files.
