docs/reviews/service-contract/codex.log:2197:docs/reviews/amendment-9/CODEX-REVIEW.md:25:   A2.1 explicitly says consensus supplies no finite bound on B − C and separates observation delay, clock error and backward timestamp skew. Neither ε = 24 h nor S = 24 h is a universal bound on how far true inclusion time can exceed a header timestamp. The predicate constrains chain timestamps against a declared time; it does not authenticate the thief’s declared time against UTC. Thus “no receipt passes with T > not-after” follows directly, but “no mint passes after true not-after plus the A2.1 skew bound” does not follow from these sources. ENCODING-V1 repeats the same unsupported inference, so agreement between the two documents is not independent evidence.
