docs/reviews/issuance-lifecycle/codex.log:14:Design review for Project Tessera at /home/tony/projects/tessera (our own repository; read-only: no repo edits, no git writes; scratch only under a fresh mktemp -d). Subject: docs/decisions/2026-10-29-issuance-lifecycle.md, the owner's plan to make the V1 issuer (service/issuer/) implement the REGISTERED issuance lifecycle instead of the owner's 24-hour FAILED rule (service resolution S4, docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:23; DEADLINE_S in service/issuer/tessera_issue/service.py). Registered sources: docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-2.md (A2.1 clock roles and timeliness latch about lines 100-160; A2.3 attempts, expiry and refusal about lines 240-300), docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md (A9.2 parameters; issuer invariant about line 422; anything in A9 that amends A2.1/A2.3 for V1), docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-3.md (refusal and delivery obligations A2.3 defers to A3, and whether A9.7 moved them out of V1), the frozen V1-PROFILE (git show 270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md) and the verifier rows 12.2/12.3 (service/verifier/tessera_verify/verify.py:236-237). Questions: (1) Does the design state the registered lifecycle correctly — N attempts, per-attempt expiry at declared + δ + S, chain-side eligibility, the latch and its precedence over expiry, explicit refusal, the window invariant? Quote the registered text for anything the design gets wrong or omits. (2) Is eligibility correctly identified with verifier rows 12.2/12.3, or does the registered eligibility predicate include more (k confirmations, A_sig anchoring, etc.)? (3) Step 4's choice to latch whenever the predicate holds before expiry is decided, including late-observed eligibility: is it permitted by A2.1 ('may be refused')? (4) The latch/expiry race and the reuse of CF2-01's write-lease rule: sound? (5) Does any registered text (A3, A9.7) make the refusal record, its delivery or its durability something V1 must do differently from 'REFUSED with a recorded reason'? (6) Do the listed owner-document changes (S4, L1, CL-03, clock-tolerance decision, DESIGN.md, fail_after) cover every place the 24-hour rule lives? grep the repo (service/, docs/) for DEADLINE_S, '24 h', '24 hours', fail_after. (7) Anything else that will bite the implementation. Number findings IL-01... with severity and the registered text. One-line verdict: is the design ready to implement. Apply these owner prechecks to the design note, PASS/FAIL with file:line:
