Two conflicts stand out: the design reduces eligibility to two timestamp checks, and its 15-minute write margin would exclude observations that A2 explicitly says must latch, including the exact boundary. A9 does narrow refusal reporting for V1 to a bounded local refusal returned by the API; I’m checking the remaining durability requirements and retry mechanics.
