docs/reviews/issuer/DISPOSITION.md:68:| CF2-01 | High | A clock check cannot bound when a write commits; the writer lease can, and it is the assumption CF-02 already rests on. `api.settle` confirms only when the decision is at least `WRITE_LEASE_S` before the deadline, so the confirmation commits before the deadline if AWS commits within the lease (stated, not established: CF3-01). Inside the last lease it leaves the request unconfirmed: it reads as ACCEPTED with its `fail_after`, and at the deadline it is FAILED. `_cleanup_one` treats an unconfirmed request as not ended, so it is cleaned up normally once settled. Cost: a request that finishes in the last 15 minutes of its 24 hours fails (S4 states about 3 hours as usual). The DESIGN.md CF-01 bullet's "no timing assumption is needed" was wrong and is corrected. | `test_CF2_01_confirmation_that_commits_late_never_reads_as_complete` (Codex's reproduction), `test_CF2_01_inside_the_last_lease_reads_as_accepted_until_the_deadline`, `test_CF2_01_a_confirmation_decided_before_the_last_lease_commits_before_the_deadline` (guards against an over-strict margin; it passes on the old code too); `test_CF01_completion_seen_before_the_deadline_never_turns_into_failed` moved to before the last lease |
